  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform string of length $L$ and mass $M$ is fixed at both ends while it is subject to a\r\ntension $T$. It can vibrate at frequencies $(v)$ given by the formula (where $n=1,2,3, \\ldots)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jX5ZM",
      "text": "$v=\\frac{n}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{T}{M L}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DjwRB",
      "text": "$v=\\frac{n}{2 L} \\sqrt{\\frac{T}{M}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3kB62",
      "text": "$v=\\frac{1}{2 n} \\sqrt{\\frac{T}{M L}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "II317",
      "text": "$v=\\frac{n}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{T L}{M}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The formula of frequency of 3 vibrations produced in tensed wire is\r\n$$\r\nv=\\frac{n}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{T}{m}}\r\n$$\r\n$m=$ Mass per unit length of the wire $=\\frac{M}{L}$\r\n$M=$ Mass of wire\r\n$L=$ Length of wire $n=$ Number of loops produced in wire $v=\\frac{n}{2 L} \\sqrt{\\frac{T}{M / L}}=\\frac{n}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{T}{M L}}$",
    "image": null
  },
